Given the context, the "initial size of the set" refers to the size of the set before the `add` operation, which can be referred to using `\old(this.size())`. The element at position `i` in the old set can be referred to using `\old(this.get(i))`.

Here is the derived assert statement:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || (this.get(i+1) != null && this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i))));</code>

This assert statement ensures that the conditions specified in the comment are met.
